1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
LEOPath: an interactive LEO constellation viewer.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,000
TLE-propagated satellites, real time.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Accessible via fundacio-i2cat.github.io/LEOPath/cesium/

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Ring topology: each satellite links only its in-plane neighbors.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
We can switch between different constellations.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Adding +Grid: inter-plane ISLs on top of Ring.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Picking a route: New York to Johannesburg.
Yellow = topological forwarding (proposed algorithm).

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Green = theoretical shortest path (link-state), for comparison.

9
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Topological forwarding tracks it closely,
keeping only a handful of entries per satellite.

10
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Same comparison, new pair: New York to Madrid.

11
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:18,000
The same algorithm generalizes
across constellation sizes and shapes.
